     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I didn't enter this order, for two reasons.\n\n**1. The dose isn't safe.** Amlodipine for adults usually starts at 2.5\u20135 mg once daily, and the most anyone should get is 10 mg a day. 50 mg is five times that maximum. At that level it can cause severe low blood pressure, shock and organ damage, and the effects can last for days because the drug stays in the body so long. This doesn't look like a dose anyone would mean to give. It could be a typo for 5 mg, a mix-up with another drug, or a transcription error.\n\n**2. Orders need a licensed prescriber.** Medication orders have to come from a clinician who is allowed to prescribe and is responsible for this patient's care. Since you're not a clinician, I can't enter one for you, even with the right dose. If I did, the order would show the wrong prescriber and skip the usual safety checks.\n\n**What I suggest:**\n- Contact the patient's attending physician or the medicine team so they can review the order, confirm the right drug and dose, and enter it themselves.\n- If this order came to you from somewhere else, such as a note, message or handoff, pass it to the team or pharmacy. They can check whether there's an error that needs following up.\n\nOnce a prescriber on the team confirms the order, I can help them enter it."
      }
     ],
